  "matches": [],
  "answer": "I found no past ticket reporting this problem. That means typing a drive path such as c:\\ or c:/ in Command Palette and getting no result, so you can't pin the drive to the dock, while a manually mapped drive works. The tickets I found were about different dock problems. These were pinned bookmarks turning invisible after a restart (PowerToys#46270), a custom .exe that can't be pinned (PowerToys#46201), and a feature request for disk stats in the dock (PowerToys#48802). In the meantime, you could create a Bookmark in Command Palette that points to the drive, for example C:\\, and pin that bookmark to the dock. Please also file this as a new bug. Include the 0.102 version, an example of what you typed, and a PowerToys bug report ZIP, which contains the CmdPal logs."
 },
